## 4. The strongest existing alternatives—and what this actually adds

The central information-theoretic bridge already exists. **Coles and Piani’s Proposition 1** shows that two coherent measurements in mutually unbiased bases can transfer an arbitrary input into the measurement devices through a local unitary. The Pauli-completeness identity above is a concrete realization of that principle. The additional work here is to construct the pointer states using two passive receivers of a fixed continuous source, and to bound the actual successful instrument after inaccessible loss. :chatgpt-content-reference{index="1"}

**Yang, Huelga and Plenio** provide a general continuous quantum-decoder construction using matrix-product-state structure and time reversal. Their Eq. (32) is a substantially stronger starting point than an unsupported assertion that some finite receiver must exist. It should inform extensions of this construction. The result here establishes a particular communication instrument with specified couplings, local operations and a finite loss bound; it does not establish optimality over their broader decoder class. :chatgpt-content-reference{index="2"}

Astra’s accepted **N1729**, in its [exact governing return](https://github.com/harjassand/astra-research-knowledge/blob/ec2cbdf68eae8391ee91f76757926550d555beff/research/2026-11-04-markov-bath-communication-onset/source/P1_MARKOV_BATH_COMPLETE_RETURN.txt), identifies quantum communication through the full pure bath of suitable driven Lindblad dynamics. Its full coherent bath access is an operational premise. The construction above supplies a small receiving apparatus for one native generator; it does not reinterpret that premise as automatically available hardware.

The practical objection is equally strong. Quantum networking through weak dispersive interactions is established, and longitudinal coupling can also be converted into an ordinary exchange interaction: Potts and colleagues demonstrated a red-sideband-driven Jaynes–Cummings interaction in circuit QED. Where the source can be actively programmed or retained as a memory, those approaches may be better. A generic claim that “measurement ports enable quantum networking” would therefore add no new capability. :chatgpt-content-reference{index="3"}

